# BKC paper trail

Anything that alters the lab environment goes through `bkc-cli` (or a BKC
pipeline it starts). That includes packages, containers, images, VMs,
services, factory proof directories, and R730/PVE executions.

Required trail: run id, command, logs, receipt. Read-only SSH inspection is
allowed. Local laptop unit tests that do not touch the lab are allowed.

Do not launch mutating worker scripts, docker runs, apt/apk, or image/HDD
builds by raw SSH. HDD stays locked until intake validation receipts exist.
Do not mutate VM145.
